Verse 1
[00:09.44]You buy bitcoin at the price you deserve
[00:11.16]So if you missed out or sold it early
[00:13.67]Well that’s the price that you paid
[00:14.86]For the tuition you earned
[00:15.93]You won’t make the mistake
[00:17.22]A second time round surely
[00:19.05]We saw the dot com bubble that bursted
[00:21.13]It took many things with it
[00:23.15]And that’s a zero sum game
[00:24.63]All fighting for fake digits
[00:25.73]It’s too big to fail
[00:26.65]And you gonna get checked
[00:28.10]You might see smoke before the fire
[00:29.90]Or get swept up and feel the impact
[00:31.56]Like a hit to the chest
[00:32.81]Might sell with sell pressure
[00:34.43]But no liquidity left
[00:35.66]At this point the only ones that get paid
[00:37.61]Are straight up owners of debt (don’t complain)
[00:40.34]Commercial lien that’s a fatal error
[00:42.28]Hate the game and still have to be a player
[00:44.06]Play it safe you still get played
[00:45.33]But learn to adapt and then play it better

Hook
[00:47.97]Money don’t grow on trees
[00:49.75]Once upon a time, printed on machines
[00:52.24]Before that, pressed out of metal
[00:54.62]And it weighed a lot
[00:55.81]So much that the bank
[00:57.26]Pressed ink on paper sheets
[00:59.32]We got your gold
[01:00.30]You can hold onto these
[01:01.60]Promissory notes were great receipts
[01:03.50]Until the bank run made them see
[01:05.58](whoo-woo)

Verse 2
